Served an exact user lookup by id or login from the identity catalog's indexes instead of reading every Profile. PAS makes that lookup for every `getUserById`, so each one cost as much as the whole site, and a listing of users or of a group's members cost the site squared: on 1,727 Profiles, one `@groups` request ran for more than seven minutes. A lookup now reads the users it returns. Substring searches, and exact searches by full name, email or name, still read every active Profile. @ericof
